." Manpage for repocompare
.TH REPOCOMPARE 1 "24 April 2026" "repocompare 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
repocompare \- Compare Debian package metadata between two APT repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B repocompare
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
repocompare fetches and parses the Packages files from two APT repositories and compares package existence and version information.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \--repo-a URL
Base URL for repo A (default from environment variable REPO_A).
.TP
.B \--repo-b URL
Base URL for repo B (default from environment variable REPO_B).
.TP
.B \--dist CODENAME
Distribution codename (e.g. bookworm).
.TP
.B \--component COMPONENT
Component name (e.g. main).
.TP
.B \--arch ARCH
Architecture (e.g. amd64).
.TP
.B \--output FORMAT
Output format: text, json, or both (default: both).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REPO_A, REPO_B
Default repository base URLs (can be set in .env or environment).
.TP
.B DIST
Default distribution codename.
.TP
.B COMPONENT
Default component name.
.TP
.B ARCH
Default architecture.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B repocompare --repo-a https://repo.example.org/ --repo-b https://repo2.example.org/ --dist bookworm --arch amd64
Compare the two repositories and print a summary and JSON output.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)

